is a dead issue,

48:06.720 --> 48:08.600
the new Congress has in fact
reintroduced

48:08.600 --> 48:09.840
a net neutrality bill,

48:11.000 --> 48:12.760
a pro-net neutrality bill, I
might add,

48:12.760 --> 48:14.080
and as long as we're talking
about it.

48:14.080 --> 48:16.400
Which is just pandering towards
constituents

48:16.400 --> 48:18.200
because they don't know what the
hell they're talking about.

48:18.200 --> 48:20.000
It's a series of tubes.

48:21.000 --> 48:23.360
So you're saying it's us that's
dumb

48:23.360 --> 48:25.520
and Ted Stevens knew what he was
talking about.

48:25.520 --> 48:26.840
He was right on the money, man.

48:26.840 --> 48:29.320
He sent the truck my way just
this morning.

48:29.360 --> 48:30.200
I got the internet.

48:30.200 --> 48:32.360
I won't work out on the smoking.

48:32.360 --> 48:33.520
There's a new bill actually.

48:33.520 --> 48:35.800
As long as we're talking about
Congress,

48:35.800 --> 48:38.360
the Senate introduced a bill
called the Platform,

48:38.360 --> 48:40.080
I should say the US Senate,

48:40.080 --> 48:42.320
introduced a bill called the
Platform Equality and Remedies

48:42.320 --> 48:43.800
for Rights Holders in Music Act,

48:43.800 --> 48:46.560
a nice acronym that stands for
Perform.

48:46.560 --> 48:47.960
This is a bill that died,

48:47.960 --> 48:51.040
an RIA bill that died last year.

48:51.040 --> 48:52.960
It would require content
protection

48:52.960 --> 48:54.880
on all satellite radio
broadcasts.

48:54.880 --> 48:56.000
You might be interested in this,
Adam,

48:56.000 --> 48:57.600
since you do stuff on Sirius,

48:57.640 --> 49:00.640
along with cable and internet
broadcasts.

49:00.640 --> 49:02.560
Broadcasters would be required
to use

49:02.560 --> 49:06.440
reasonably available and
economically reasonable
technology

49:06.440 --> 49:09.000
to prevent music theft.

49:09.000 --> 49:12.040
Another misunderstood
conversation

49:12.040 --> 49:15.000
that has produced a knee-jerk
reaction.

49:15.000 --> 49:17.640
Well, you've done a lot for
PodSafe music

49:17.640 --> 49:20.040
with your PodSafe network.

49:20.040 --> 49:21.640
Exactly, that's the point.

49:21.640 --> 49:23.760
And that's what this is about.

49:23.760 --> 49:25.960
It's about licensing and money.

49:26.000 --> 49:29.760
There's huge forces at work who
make money

49:29.760 --> 49:32.880
based upon the reuse of content,

49:32.880 --> 49:35.520
musical works, the publishing
predominantly,

49:35.520 --> 49:38.720
but also the duplication rights.

49:38.720 --> 49:41.160
And it's always been a nice
little game.

49:41.160 --> 49:43.360
You have the 6,000 radio
stations,

49:43.360 --> 49:44.600
they all have to pay X amount

49:44.600 --> 49:46.840
based upon how many listeners
they have.

49:46.840 --> 49:48.520
And the way that money is
divided

49:48.520 --> 49:51.360
within the performing rights
societies,

49:51.360 --> 49:55.400
ASCAP BMI has always been a very
fuzzy black box,

49:55.400 --> 49:57.000
let the people who want to make
money

49:57.000 --> 49:57.960
are making the money.

49:57.960 --> 50:02.040
And what the PodSafe music
revolution did is said,

50:02.040 --> 50:05.520
hey, that's fine, we want your
stuff protected

50:05.520 --> 50:08.200
and we don't necessarily believe
in DRM.

50:08.200 --> 50:13.200
So trust your co-license
agreement partners

50:13.200 --> 50:17.240
on this, mainly podcasters, and
give your stuff for free.

50:17.240 --> 50:20.040
And let them play it and we'll
tell you

50:20.040 --> 50:22.040
when it was played and then you
can go

50:22.040 --> 50:25.120
and build your business and
everything's fair.

50:25.160 --> 50:27.000
There's no money exchanging
hands though.

50:27.000 --> 50:30.080
So it's only about licensure?

50:30.080 --> 50:32.960
It's merely just so that they
know what's going on.

50:32.960 --> 50:34.600
I mean, they're getting value in
terms

50:34.600 --> 50:35.600
of promotional value.

50:37.400 --> 50:42.400
They're getting huge value and
not just financial value,

50:42.600 --> 50:45.760
